# Encodings the standard allows but a canonical encoder would not write: a
# length spelled long, a tag number escaped needlessly, an integer with
# leading octets it does not need. Each decodes to its value and re-encodes
# to exactly these octets; only a fresh, canonical encoding is shorter.

25 01 48 => unsigned 72 (non-canonical)
22 00 48 => unsigned 72 (long)
32 ff b8 => signed -72 (long)
f9 02 48 => [2] 48 (non-canonical)
f2 02 00 01 => unsigned 1 (non-canonical)
# Escape 5 with a one-octet length: legal, long, and easy to misread as five
# octets of contents. It is one octet, then three NULLs.
95 01 00 00 00 00 => enumerated 0 (non-canonical), null, null, null
